\f1\fs22 The Very Arch Bishop d\'92Molesto addressed the congregation.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Dearly invested, we are gathered here today, in sight of the Nine Major Saints of Latter Day Capitalism, to witness and celebrate the exchange of contracts between these two counter parties, Sarah Jacobson and Alexander Koalemos, in the matter of holy joint venture. We praise the perfection of the Market and render up our forecasts in thanks-giving, trusting they will always be truer than throwing a dart at a board. May your enterprises be always too big to fail.\'92\

\f2\i <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91And also yours.\'92
\f1\i0 \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91And I say unto you, it is easier for a camel to pass through the security checkpoint of an investment bank than it is for a rich person to allow a poor person a dollar.\'92\

\f2\i <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91They don\'92t deserve it.\'92
\f1\i0 \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The Very Arch Bishop opened the extremely heavy bible and scowled, mildly annoyed that he needed to flick a few pages forward and back to find his place. He usually nailed the right page for scripture readings as common as these.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91From the New Ulyssian Market Bible, the first reading is from Exploitations, Chapter 1.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91In the beginning, the Market created the heavens and the earth, and the Market moved over the earth. Then the Market said, \'93Let there be privilege\'94; and there was privilege. The Market saw that privilege was good, and separated the privileged from under-privileged.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Then the Market said, \'93Let Us cast humanity in Our image, according to Our perfection; and let them exploit the fish and the birds and the cattle and every creeping thing.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91The Market moulded humanity in Its own image, in the image of the Market It moulded them, into the chosen and the reviled. And to the chosen the Market said, \'93Go forth and multiply your assets; fill the earth and subdue it; rule over every living thing, and exploit every resource I have given you. Cut and burn and extract and consume all I have given you.\'94\'92\

\f2\i <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91May your taxes be small and your margins large,\'92
\f1\i0  the Airborne in the congregation chanted. The Elvi sat dumbfounded, soaking up every nuance of the ritual as if it was life-giving elixir.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91And from St Rupert\'92s 2
\fs14 \super nd
\fs22 \nosupersub  email to the Corinthians, Chapter 5: \'93Therefore anyone of the Market is a new creature; old indiscretions are buried and forgotten; behold, fresh opportunities arise.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91And finally from St Rupert\'92s 1
\fs14 \super st
\fs22 \nosupersub  email to the Corinthians, Chapter 13: \'93The Market is impatient; the Market is ruthless and jealous; the Market brags and is arrogant. It is easily provoked, keeps account for wrongs suffered
\f2\i ,
\f1\i0  rejoices in quick wins, and kicks truth down the road. It bears all things, believes all things, hopes all things, exploits all things.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The Very Arch Bishop closed the bible; the Airborne in the congregation fondled their jewellery; the Elvi combed their hair and straightened their sunglasses.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The Bishop came down from the pulpit and stood before the happy couple, saying, \'91Sarah and Alexander, will you honour the sacred charge of joint venturers, and together seal and harden your resolve for profit, in prosperity and tax audit, in price gouging and cashflow crisis?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91We will.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91And now for the exchanging of cheques.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The was a brief pause while Sarah elbowed Alexander, prompting him to recite his lines.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91With this cheque, I, Alexander Koalemos, take you, Sarah Jacobson, as my lawfully contracted counter party in holy joint venture, to have and to hold accountable, for better or much better, for richer or even richer, for as long as we both remain solvent.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Restrained, self-entitled tittering could be heard among the congregation; no Airborne ever became insolvent.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>After a pregnant pause, Sarah placed a small poly-paper cheque (not refundable in South Ulyssia) in Alexander\'92s hand and said, \'91Yeah, me too.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable> \'91Let the cheques be cashed,\'92 declared Bishop d\'92Molesto, as the happy couple folded their cheques into gold wallets. \'91I now pronounce you joint venturers. You may celebrate the deal.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>When Alexander lifted the black veil and revealed Sarah\'92s face, everyone held their breaths in collective awe and joy. It was later agreed no one had seen a lovelier, healthier counter  party.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Alexander shook with nerves, yet steadied enough to lean in and peck Sarah\'92s lips. He was already anticipating how good he\'92d look in the celebration vids with Sarah on his arm.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The congregation rose and applauded.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The Elvi cheered and began singing. Their hips swayed and there was not a dry eye behind their dark sunglasses. \'91All praise the Holy Momma of the New Church of the One After the One!\'92 they declared.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Praise the Holy Momma!\'92 they chanted over and over.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Dunhilton dug his fingernails deep into the varnish of the pew in front of him.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Praise the Holy Momma!\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Dunhilton\'92s knuckles turned white as he stared threats of dismemberment at the Very Arch Bishop.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Bishop d\'92Molesto was struck to the core with fear.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Unable to contain himself, Dunhilton marched on d\'92Molesto and drew near enough to his ear. \'91Do you realise what you\'92ve done? You\'92ve exposed these clones to religion! Sweet Jesus Salt and Vinegar Chips, doesn\'92t anyone read a warranty card any more?\'92
